    "area_or_other_cost": "Area increases because each 32-bit adder now uses three 16-bit adders and a mux instead of one 32-bit ripple adder. Adder combinational logic grows by about 50% per adder; overall module area is estimated to increase by 20-30%. No additional registers are required.",
    "functional_boundaries": "Preserves the module name 'timing_adder', all input/output ports, active-low asynchronous reset semantics, nonblocking pipeline behavior, exact cycle-by-cycle output latency, and modulo 2^32 arithmetic.",
    "bottleneck": "The critical path is from b[0] to the sum1 flip-flop (endpoint _541_) through a 32-bit ripple-carry adder chain (many maj3 cells) with data arrival time 8.39 ns and worst slack 1.38 ns. A similar long path exists from c[0] to the sum2 flip-flop.",
    "rewrite": "Replaced the two 32-bit ripple-carry adders (a+b and sum1+c) with carry-select adders. Each 32-bit carry-select adder splits the addition into a 16-bit lower half and two 16-bit upper halves (with carry-in 0 and 1), then muxes the upper result based on the lower half carry-out. This halves the carry propagation chain length from 32 bits to 16 bits plus a mux.",
    "expected_timing_gain": "Approximately 40-50% reduction in critical path delay for both adder paths. Data arrival time is expected to drop from ~8.4 ns to ~4.5-5.0 ns, improving the worst slack from 1.38 ns to >4.5 ns (a gain of roughly 3.5-4 ns)."
